      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{27(x-1)^{3}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{27(x-1)^{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{3(x-1)\\cdot 3(x-1)\\cdot 3(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(3(x-1))}^{3}} & = \\\\ 3(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
